# FFLib (Salesforce Enterprise Patterns) – Best Practices

## Core Principles

1. **One transaction → one UOW → one commit**
2. **All DML through UOW** (no direct DML when a UOW exists)
3. **Layering:**
   - **Controllers / triggers / batch / queueables** = entry points (may create + commit UOW)
   - **Services** = orchestration only, use existing UOW
   - **Domains** = business logic on records, no UOW, no queries
   - **Selectors** = data access only, no logic, no DML

---

## 1. Unit of Work (UOW) Pattern Rules

### 1.1 ONE UOW Per Transaction

**Never create and commit multiple UOWs in the same transaction.**

❌ **Bad – multiple commits & multiple UOWs:**

```apex
public void processRecords() {
    // First commit
    fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow1 = Application.UOWContext.createNewUOW();
    uow1.registerDirty(someRecord);
    Application.UOWContext.removeCurrentUOW().commitWork(); // ❌ commit 1
    
    // Second commit
    fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow2 = Application.UOWContext.createNewUOW();
    uow2.registerDirty(anotherRecord);
    Application.UOWContext.removeCurrentUOW().commitWork(); // ❌ commit 2
}
```

✅ **Good – one UOW, one commit:**

```apex
public void processRecords() {
    fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow = Application.UOWContext.getCurrentUOW();
    
    uow.registerDirty(someRecord);
    uow.registerDirty(anotherRecord);
    
    // Commit once at the end (by the caller / entry point)
}
```

### 1.2 Where to Create UOW – Controllers / Triggers Only

**Entry points** (Aura/LWC controllers, REST endpoints, batch/queueable, triggers) create the UOW and commit.

**Services and domains must not create or commit.**

✅ **Controller – creates and commits UOW:**

```apex
@AuraEnabled
public static void saveData(String jsonData) {
    Id recordId;
    fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow;
    
    try {
        uow = Application.UOWContext.createNewUOW();
        
        Data data = (Data) JSON.deserialize(jsonData, Data.class);
        recordId = data.recordId;
        
        OpportunityServiceImpl service = new OpportunityServiceImpl();
        service.processSomething(recordId);  // uses current UOW
        
        uow.commitWork();
        
    } catch (DmlException ex) {
        Log.exception('Error processing recordId: ' + recordId, ex);
        throw new AuraHandledException(ex.getMessage());
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        Log.exception('General exception for recordId: ' + recordId, ex);
        throw new AuraHandledException('Error saving: ' + ex.getMessage());
    } finally {
        // ✅ always clear context
        Application.UOWContext.removeCurrentUOW();
    }
}
```

✅ **Service – uses existing UOW (no create/commit):**

```apex
public class OpportunityServiceImpl implements IOpportunityService {
    public void processOpportunities(List<Opportunity> opps, Map<Id, SObject> existingRecords) {
        fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow = Application.UOWContext.getCurrentUOW();
        
        for (Opportunity opp : opps) {
            // Business logic here
        }
        
        uow.registerDirty(opps);
        // ✅ no commit here
    }
}
```

### 1.3 Pass UOW Into Helpers (Don't Hide getCurrentUOW())

Instead of every helper calling `getCurrentUOW()` itself, **pass the UOW in from the service**.

❌ **Bad – helper silently calls getCurrentUOW():**

```apex
private static void createRecords(List<SObject> records) {
    fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow = Application.UOWContext.getCurrentUOW();
    uow.registerNew(records);
}
```

✅ **Good – helper receives UOW:**

```apex
private static void createRecords(List<SObject> records, fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow) {
    if (records.isEmpty() || uow == null) {
        return;
    }
    uow.registerNew(records);
}
```

### 1.4 Consolidate Updates for the Same Record

When multiple pieces of logic want to update the same record, use a Map to combine changes and register once.

```apex
Map<Id, Opportunity> oppsToUpdate = new Map<Id, Opportunity>();

for (Opportunity opp : opportunityList) {
    Opportunity oppUpdate = oppsToUpdate.containsKey(opp.Id) 
        ? oppsToUpdate.get(opp.Id) 
        : new Opportunity(Id = opp.Id);
    
    oppUpdate.SomeField__c = 'value';
    oppsToUpdate.put(opp.Id, oppUpdate);
}

uow.registerDirty(oppsToUpdate.values());
```

