## 2. Selector & Bulkification Rules

### 2.1 No Selectors Inside Loops

❌ **Bad – SOQL in loop:**

```apex
for (Opportunity opp : opportunityList) {
    Goal__c goal = GoalsSelector.newInstance()
        .selectByStage(opp.StageName); // ❌ SOQL in loop
}
```

✅ **Good – bulkified with one selector call + map:**

```apex
// Collect unique values
Set<String> stageNames = new Set<String>();
for (Opportunity opp : opportunityList) {
    stageNames.add(opp.StageName);
}

// Bulk selector call
Map<String, Goal__c> goalsByStage = GoalsSelector.newInstance()
    .selectByStagesAsMap(stageNames);

// Use map in loop
for (Opportunity opp : opportunityList) {
    Goal__c goal = goalsByStage.get(opp.StageName);
}
```

### 2.2 Query All Required Fields Upfront

Extend selector methods to return all needed fields, don't add ad-hoc SOQL in services.

```apex
public List<Fixture__c> selectByIdWithTeams(Set<Id> fixtureIds) {
    fflib_QueryFactory queryFactory = newQueryFactory()
        .setCondition('Id IN :fixtureIds');
    
    // Include related records
    new TeamsSelector().configureQueryFactoryFields(queryFactory, 'Home_Team__r');
    new TeamsSelector().configureQueryFactoryFields(queryFactory, 'Away_Team__r');
    
    return (List<Fixture__c>) Database.query(queryFactory.toSOQL());
}
```

