## 9. Testing Best Practices

### Unit Tests (With Mocks) - Fast & Isolated

```apex
@IsTest
static void givenValidRecords_whenProcessing_thenRegistersCorrectly() {
    // Given - Mock selectors
    fflib_ApexMocks mocks = new fflib_ApexMocks();
    IFixturesSelector mockSelector = (IFixturesSelector) mocks.mock(IFixturesSelector.class);
    
    mocks.startStubbing();
    mocks.when(mockSelector.selectById(fflib_Match.anySet()))
        .thenReturn(new List<Fixture__c>());
    mocks.stopStubbing();
    
    Application.Selector.setMock(mockSelector);
    
    // When
    Test.startTest();
    Application.UOWContext.createNewUOW();
    
    MyService.processRecords(recordIds);
    
    Application.UOWContext.commitAndCleanup();
    Test.stopTest();
    
    // Then - Verify
    ((IFixturesSelector) mocks.verify(mockSelector, 1))
        .selectById(fflib_Match.anySet());
}
```

### Integration Tests (With Real Data) - Catches Trigger Chains

```apex
@IsTest
static void givenRealData_whenProcessing_thenAllTriggersWork() {
    // Given - Create REAL records
    Account team = TestDataFactory.createTeam('Test Team');
    Fixture__c fixture = TestDataFactory.createFixture(team.Id);
    
    // When - NO MOCKS, let real triggers fire
    Test.startTest();
    fixture.Status__c = 'Completed';
    update fixture;
    Test.stopTest();
    
    // Then - Query database and verify
    Fixture__c updated = [SELECT Status__c FROM Fixture__c WHERE Id = :fixture.Id];
    System.assertEquals('Completed', updated.Status__c);
}
```

